1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:00,560
wait...

2
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,740
you're eating that?

3
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:03,020
the date on the bag

4
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:04,260
was yesterday!

5
00:00:04,430 --> 00:00:05,900
and who decided yesterday

6
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:07,150
was the day?

7
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:07,920
the date did.

8
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:09,310
it's printed right here.

9
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:10,460
read it to me.

10
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:11,490
best...

11
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:12,550
before.

12
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:13,880
before what?

13
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,310
i always read it as...

14
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:16,880
“bad after.”

15
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,430
most people do.

16
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,450
watch this.

17
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:23,050
the date is chosen

18
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:23,800
by the people

19
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:25,310
who make the food.

20
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,230
“best before” is about quality,

21
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,440
not safety.

22
00:00:28,610 --> 00:00:29,460
after that,

23
00:00:29,610 --> 00:00:31,870
food may be less perfect.

24
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:33,410
stored right,

25
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:34,950
it's still safe.

26
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,260
but many of us read

27
00:00:36,290 --> 00:00:38,630
it as “bad after”...

28
00:00:38,990 --> 00:00:40,800
and in it goes.

29
00:00:40,970 --> 00:00:42,540
UK homes throw away

30
00:00:42,570 --> 00:00:44,940
about 4.4 million tonnes

31
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:46,730
of good food a year.

32
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,500
in 2022,

33
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:50,760
big UK supermarkets took

34
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:53,280
“best before” off hundreds

35
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:54,540
of fruit and veg.

36
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:57,760
but “use by” is different.

37
00:00:58,020 --> 00:00:59,940
that one is about safety.

38
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,640
never eat past it.

39
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:04,800
so i've been binning

40
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:05,660
good food...

41
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:07,400
because i misread one word.

42
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,800
most of what we bin

43
00:01:09,830 --> 00:01:11,200
isn't spoiled.

44
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:12,910
just misread.

45
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:14,480
use by:

46
00:01:14,510 --> 00:01:15,500
respect it.

47
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:16,890
best before:

48
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:17,780
check it.

49
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:19,500
so...

50
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,350
open your fridge tonight.

51
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:22,130
which date

52
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,810
have you been misreading?

